{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.OddDecayWeightParity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.OddDecayWeightParity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.ZBarParity"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.OddDecayWeightParity.classical_shadow_on_even_face","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.OddDecayWeightParity.classical_shadow_on_even_face","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OddDecayWeightParity.lean#L100-L115","doc":"**The classical mass content is carried by the even face.** For the graded\nsplit `qCubic = e + c` with `e` the bar-EVEN even/mass face (`σ e = e`) and\n`c = g · γ` the bar-ODD odd/mixing cross-term, every bar-compatible\nevaluation `φ` into a characteristic-`≠ 2` field satisfies `φ(qCubic) = φ(e)`:\nthe nonzero q=1 (classical) shadow of the q-cubic is sourced ENTIRELY by the\nbar-even even face, never by the pure bar-odd mixing sector. This is the\nnecessary condition on the open wall `q_cubic = C1` — the mass/binding\nclassical content must live on the even (C1/cosh) block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.OddDecayWeightParity.crossTerm_shadow_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.OddDecayWeightParity.crossTerm_shadow_zero","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OddDecayWeightParity.lean#L88-L98","doc":"**The mixing cross-term `c₃` has vanishing q=1 shadow.** Being bar-odd\n(`crossTerm_bar_odd`), the cross-term `c = g · γ` is annihilated by every\nbar-compatible evaluation `φ`: `2·φ(c) = 0`. Hence the c₃ \"`−2 = J_Hopf(1)`\"\nclassical near-match is NOT the pure Berezinian cross-term evaluated at q=1 —\nthat evaluation is forced to zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.OddDecayWeightParity.crossTerm_bar_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.OddDecayWeightParity.crossTerm_bar_odd","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OddDecayWeightParity.lean#L79-L86","doc":"**The first even/odd mixing cross-term is bar-ODD.** Model the Berezinian\ncross-term `B·D⁻¹·C` as `c = g · γ`, where `g` is the bar-EVEN even-block\ndressing (the scalar assembled from the even C1/mass block, `σ g = g`) and\n`γ` the bar-ODD odd-face weight. A single even/odd mixing flips the\nbar-parity: `σ c = −c` (`bar_even_mul_bar_odd`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.OddDecayWeightParity.oddWeight_shadow_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.OddDecayWeightParity.oddWeight_shadow_zero","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OddDecayWeightParity.lean#L68-L77","doc":"**The odd decay weight has vanishing q=1 shadow.** For every bar-compatible\nevaluation `φ` (`φ ∘ σ = φ`, e.g. the q=1 / classical shadow), the exactly\nbar-odd odd-face weight `γ` satisfies `2·φ(γ) = 0` — division-free; over a\ntarget of characteristic `≠ 2` this is `φ(γ) = 0`. The GGM/decay face\ncontributes nothing at the bar-fixed point. Direct from\n`fixed_eval_two_mul_kills_bar_odd`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.OddDecayWeightParity.IsOddFaceWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.OddDecayWeightParity.IsOddFaceWeight","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/OddDecayWeightParity.lean#L62-L66","doc":"**Bar-oddness of the odd/decay face weight.** Abbreviation matching the\nDoor-v `(−1)^m` GGM alternation: `σ γ = −γ`. Kept as a plain predicate (no\nclass carrier) — the hypothesis is an on-`main` established fact\n(`QOU.Mass.DoorVParityNoIdentity`), threaded explicitly. ","signatureChunk":0}]}